   "text": {
    "L1": "Today we will compare weights using grams and kilograms.",
    "L2": "A bigger-looking object is not always heavier. Only weighing and comparing tells us.",
    "L3": "Here is the key fact: 1 kilogram is 1000 grams.",
    "L4": "To compare weights, first change them to the same unit.",
    "L5": "For example, change 1 kilogram 300 grams into grams.",
    "L6": "That is 1000 grams plus 300 grams, or 1300 grams.",
    "L7": "Now compare 1300 grams with 1250 grams. The flour is heavier by 50 grams.",
    "L8": "Your turn: tap the heavier weight in the example."
   },
